{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/641118-creating-an-iron-chef-archetype-garou-character","id":641118,"title":"Creating an \"Iron Chef\" Archetype Garou Character","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-26T22:16:11-07:00","id":641118,"title":"Creating an \"Iron Chef\" Archetype Garou Character","content":"A combination of watching Chef Ramsey and watching the Anime &quot;Shougeki No Souma: Food Wars&quot;, not to mention reading its Manga Adaptation and the Werewolf 20 Cookbook in close proximation has me suddenly REALLY wanting to play a Garou whose defining character concept is that of the &quot;Iron Chef.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, a few starting points for discussion:<br /> <br /> 1) Personally I believe that as an art (and an occasional performing art) the Galliard would the most appropriate Auspice for one who makes cooking his life:<br /> But would any other Auspices be appropriate for the life of a Chef? And how would THEY approach the Sweet Science of Taste?<br /> <br /> 2) From tribe to tribe (and auspice accordingly) how would I go about creating the Chef(s) in question?<br /> And no, before anyone starts, even though I love Stargazers I do NOT intend to play the &quot;screaming shouting fish chopping chef in Chinatown&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 3) As that film just happens to be playing on Disney Channel in the background, I suddenly came up with the concept of a menacing Shadow-Lord Italian-Chef dressed in fine funeral clothes based on Anton Ego the food-critic from &quot;Ratatouille&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> How does that sound? And for that matter what Auspice would someone as cold and dull as Anton Ego be?<br /> <br /> Let the delivious fun begin! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T08:28:47-07:00","id":643021,"title":"","content":"I don't have much, but:<br /> <br /> 1) A Ragabash cook might try to bend and break the rules of what goes well together and create some avantgarde meals. Or a Theurge cooking guru who gets the freshest ingredients from his Awakened herb garden and produces some incredible health food, perhaps even educates the human public on &quot;you are what you eat&quot;?<br /> 3) Ego is bascially a judge in the movie, so Philodox offers itself.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T08:36:37-07:00","id":643027,"title":"","content":"And an Ahroun could still outcook Bobby Flay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T08:40:00-07:00","id":643029,"title":"","content":"1: I don't think you have to be a certain auspice to cook. Being a Galliard would help but not necessary.<br /> <br /> 2: Go nuts. Most are pretty self explanitory while others are open to interpretation.<br /> <br /> 3: The Auspice, I would say Philodox. Your not the only one who's taken inspiration from media. I made the bum from Werewolf (the tv series).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T11:22:24-07:00","id":643195,"title":"","content":"1- Every auspice: <b>ragabash</b>, maybe he is subtle in some ways, he stole recipes from other famous chef and he's trying to made them better with spirits aid.<br /> <b>theurge</b>, who use spirits and fetish-crafting to restore health and morale among the local garou, maybe it's just is way to ward and heal the caern<br /> <b>philodox</b>, most difficult. Maybe a social-leader who seek balance in everything, even in food, maybe he is a caern-chef, findind the right food for every garou and every role-sept, more proteins for the guardians and warders, less food for shamanic roles ecc.<br /> <b>Galliard - </b>off course he's an artist, or maybe he's searching for ancient recipes among humans and tribes, to create new special food for every garou to remember them their origins and traditions. Maybe he is a straight traditionalist<br /> <b>Ahroun- </b>He channel his rage with food ideas and creation. Maybe without the galliard ideas, but with great amount of food, grilled meat, salt pork ecc. Maybe he is the camp-chef during some missions.<br /> <br /> 2- I have a lot of ideas... really a lot, too muche, by the way:<br /> <b>Bone Gnawers:</b> maybe he is some kind of famous guy among the bg, he know how to cook something very rare for a bone gnawers, something very good to eat. Ragabash of course, he need to steal from other tribes, changing breeds or restourants. Mental/physical but keep in mind charisma or manipulation with freebie points<br /> <b>Get of Fenris: </b>Galliard, traditionalist, a masterchief with fish, sausages and potatoes, he know every german-scandinavian typical recipes from the coast. He always will remember to his pakmates his tribe tradition and why he cook it. And of course, if it is time to die, you have to eat something very good before the glory. He know how to make blood taste better.<br /> <b>Glass Walker: </b>theurge. He has a lot of kitchen-tech-tools and spirits who help him to make perfect food. Maybe a special cook-fetish or something similar. He's a real master with modern food and recipes. Always punctual with food.<br /> <b>Shadow Lords: </b>Philodox. Damn cunning guy. Cold but smiling, friendly but bastard. He never, NEVER, fail with salt, pepper, and other quantity for his food, his cuisine is perfect and balanced. He know every italian and french recipes and he's trying to create the perfect cuisine for the whole garou nation. And he's ready to cheat for his achievements.<br /> <b>Silver Fangs</b>: Ahroun. Gordon Ramsey-style with other kinfolk under him. He will not allow them to fail. Never. He's food is the best in the caern. He's also a brawler and a hot-headed warrior who care of food during mission against the wyrm. Maybe he's specialized in hig-rank cuisine, like lobster, fish and rare meat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T07:48:39-07:00","id":653913,"title":"","content":"One of my players has toyed with this concept for awhile now. He was leaning towards Uktena Galliard who specializes in traditional cuisines infused with modern takes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}